### **Bug 5: Late-Arriving Events Counted Twice (log.js)**

**Problem:** When an event arrived out of order (late), it was being appended to BOTH the main `events` array AND the `late` array. This caused it to be counted twice when replaying in canonical order.

**Fix:** Modified `append()` to put events exclusively in either `events` (if in order) or `late` (if out of order), not both:

```javascript
append(event) {
  if (this.maxAt !== null && event.at < this.maxAt) {
    // Event arrived out of order; track it separately for auditing.
    this.late.push(event)
  } else {
    // Event arrived in order; keep it in the main array.
    this.events.push(event)
  }
  if (this.maxAt === null || event.at > this.maxAt) this.maxAt = event.at
}
```

