### 4. **Wheelchair Space Fallback Logic Flawed** (`src/allocator.js`)
**Issue**: The `standardSoldOut()` function only checked if all standard seats were individually blocked, not whether any row could provide a **contiguous block** of the requested size. Per the docs: "Accessible seats are released to a general request **only when no row offers a contiguous run of free standard seats of the requested size**"

**Impact**: "Wheelchair spaces never open up for general sale even when standard seating can no longer take the group"

**Fix**: Replaced `standardSoldOut()` with `hasStandardBlock()` that properly checks for contiguous availability:
```javascript
function hasStandardBlock(venue, { size, blocked }) {
  return venue.rows.some((row) => {
    const free = new Set(
      row.seats
        .filter((s) => s.kind === 'standard' && !blocked.has(seatLabel(row.id, s.n)))
        .map((s) => s.n),
    )
    for (const n of free) {
      const run = []
      for (let k = 0; k < size; k++) run.push(n + k)
      if (run.every((m) => free.has(m)) && isContiguous(row, run)) {
        return true
      }
    }
    return false
  })
}
```

